From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Murgola <andy@murgo.la>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:36:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] moe: pinned parallel staging for the uploads of host
 experts

Host experts are memory-mapped and pageable, so every upload was a synchronous
driver copy soft-faulting the mapping page by page on one thread (2 to 3 GB/s,
less from disk). llama_host_stager copies the source into a pinned buffer on
several threads, the device reads it asynchronously while the threads fill the
other buffer, and the pages of a large batch are read at low memory priority
so a prompt scan no longer evicts the experts generation keeps hitting.
Default 128 MiB x 2 per GPU for models with host experts (--moe-stage-mib).
